Check pipe2 with its real declaration so the compiler can enforce the SDK's
deployment-target availability annotation. A headerless has_function() probe
uses its own declaration and can incorrectly enable HAVE_PIPE2 for macOS 15
when building against a macOS 27 SDK. Keep _GNU_SOURCE for Linux detection.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -834,5 +834,8 @@
 foreach f : functions
-  if cc.has_function(f)
+  # The SDK declaration carries pipe2's deployment-target availability.
+  # A headerless probe can link a symbol which is unavailable at runtime.
+  prefix = f == 'pipe2' ? '#define _GNU_SOURCE\n#include <unistd.h>' : ''
+  if cc.has_function(f, prefix: prefix)
     define = 'HAVE_' + f.underscorify().to_upper()
     glib_conf.set(define, 1)
     glib_conf_prefix = glib_conf_prefix + '#define @0@ 1\n'.format(define)
